Android SDK Requirements
------------------------

The build worked with:

- Android SDK platform `android-33`
- Android SDK build-tools `33.0.1`
- Android SDK CMake `3.22.1`

Important:

ffmpeg-kit's Android scripts look for CMake inside
`ANDROID_SDK_ROOT/cmake/...` before checking `PATH`.

CMake 4 fails to configure `cpu-features` ("Compatibility with CMake < 3.5 has
been removed"). Keep SDK CMake `3.22.1` installed. The scripts take the first
`cmake` they find under `ANDROID_SDK_ROOT/cmake` (`android_ndk_cmake` in
`scripts/function-android.sh`), not the one on `PATH`, so when a CMake 4 is
installed there as well, export `CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5` before
building.

A Safari-downloaded NDK carries the quarantine flag, and macOS then refuses to
load its toolchain libraries. Clear it once after unpacking:

```sh
xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine "$HOME/Library/Android/ndk/android-ndk-r25d-canary"
```

The working SDK CMake path was:

`/Users/renetik/Library/Android/sdk/cmake/3.22.1/bin/cmake`

